Great.  Someone has actually used our archetype BAI cmavo.

I more or less agree that the tu'a would be preferred.  Historically, the
BAIs were not so rigidly tied to the place structures, but instead relied
on them for general semantic guidelines.  The language has evolved towards
matching place structures, and the closer the match, the more that the
semantics of the places applies to the BAI-tagged sumti.

